WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.060
SPEAKER 1: Do you see
now how the first check

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.120
on the government is
that we must consent?

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:11.118
But the second check is that
we do not run the government.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.930
In America, in the government
of the United States,

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.720
in the federal
government, what is

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.560
it that the people do
absolutely none of?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.363
AUDIENCE: Make the laws.

00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:29.030
AUDIENCE: Creating
the judiciary branch.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.530
AUDIENCE: Enforcing the laws.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.000
SPEAKER 1: They are not judges.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.680
They are not legislators.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.890
And they are not
executives over the law.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.210
They are entirely excluded
from the operation

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.030
of the government.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.350
Isn't that odd?

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.130
Right?

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.950
In England and Great
Britain, at the time

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.518
of the American Revolution,
who was the executive?

00:00:56.518 --> 00:00:57.310
AUDIENCE: The king.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:58.490
AUDIENCE: The king.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.710
SPEAKER 1: And his
ministers, right?

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.985
And who was the sovereign?

00:01:01.985 --> 00:01:03.797
AUDIENCE: The king.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.840
SPEAKER 1: The king, right?

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.200
So the one possessing
legitimate title to rule

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.880
occupied the executive branch.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.425
In Athens, who was
the legislature?

00:01:13.425 --> 00:01:14.300
AUDIENCE: The people.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.217
SPEAKER 1: The people.

00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.265
And who was the sovereign?

00:01:17.265 --> 00:01:18.140
AUDIENCE: The people.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.190
SPEAKER 1: The people.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:20.660
Athens, just the
people would meet,

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.730
and they were always
changing their mind.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:28.370
And so in America,
it is different

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:34.460
because unlike Athens, unlike
England, all the sovereignty

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.490
is ours.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.730
We may not be governed
except by our consent.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.120
And if we don't give
it, no governing.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.270
All government is
illegitimate except with that.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.610
And of course, it
follows from that that

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:52.670
in the practical operation of
the government, since unanimity

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.950
is impossible, majority rule.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.810
And of course, in a college--

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.580
in a proper college--

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.120
if you disagree,
somebody's wrong.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.700
We're here to find out who's
wrong, and who's right.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.160
Well, we always disagree.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.289
How are we ever going
to figure it out, right?

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:12.830
But yeah, so there's
going to be voting,

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.680
and there's going
to be disagreement,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.420
and we're not going
to reach unanimity.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.480
Why is the majority
the right thing?

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.400
AUDIENCE: It seems
like it's more probable

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.250
that more people, since
it's not a mob at that time

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.520
because they're voting on
something in a republican

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.170
fashion, that they would have
considered it in a way that

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.065
would refine their opinions.

00:02:39.065 --> 00:02:40.565
SPEAKER 1: Ooh,
that's really novel.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.090
I don't think it's true.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.260
All men are created equal.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.840
You got 300 people.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.050
160 want to do A,
and 140 want to do

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.290
not A. If you do
what the 140 says,

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.470
you've got yourself
an aristocracy, right?

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.780
In other words, the
majority of equal souls

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.640
has to stand in for
the unanimous consent.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.760
And in anything not
fundamental or anything

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.070
that involves the ongoing
operation of the government,

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.440
that's what you need, see?

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.190
So the point is, you're going
to have majorities rule.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:20.560
You're going to
have representation.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.570
And that gives rise
to something new.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.330
And Madison says that it's
never happened before.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.360
It's unique.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.620
The sovereign is the people
as expressed by what--

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.370
I'll introduce a new phrase
that Abraham Lincoln liked--

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.500
"The people, as they
express their wealth

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.140
through their
constitutional majority,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.270
is the only true sovereign
of a free people."

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.880
And so that's where
sovereignty is.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:54.250
That's where the right to say
the legitimate title to rule

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.050
is.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:59.080
But those people, the
sovereign, are entirely

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:03.190
excluded from the operation
of the government.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.430
Do you see now how the first
check on the government

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.160
is that we must consent?

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.140
But the second check
on the government

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.770
is that we who have
the power to consent

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.790
do not run the government.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:23.230
And that second check
is a check on us.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:28.810
The federalist answer is that
every human exercise of power

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.600
must be restrained by reason.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.700
And there are
constitutional forms

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:37.180
that have to be implemented
that can help bring that out.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.580
And if the first
constitutional form

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.580
is representation,
the method by which we

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.300
give our ongoing
consent, the second

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:52.720
is the separation between
sovereignty and power.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.730
So you get consent.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.790
And that gives rise
to representation.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.830
And that gives rise
to a separation

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.740
between the sovereign
and the government.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:11.620
And Madison says this has
never been done before.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.070
SPEAKER 2: Thank
you for watching.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:15.040
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlights series

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.920
and invite you to explore
